From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:43:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: only report implemented low-power support

SupportManager unconditionally advertises LOW_POWER, even when the device
has neither a LOW_POWER hint nor an ADPF profile. The generic setMode path
then has no implementation for that mode.

Use the existing hint/profile checks for LOW_POWER, like other modes.
Device-specific implementations can still report support through the
existing override checked first by Power::isModeSupported.

Base: 13281f8a0d718205781245f27ded74bc5ff03388
Source: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_hardware_lineage_interfaces/blob/13281f8a0d718205781245f27ded74bc5ff03388/power-libperfmgr/aidl/SupportManager.cpp
Signed-off-by: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
---
 power-libperfmgr/aidl/SupportManager.cpp | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/power-libperfmgr/aidl/SupportManager.cpp b/power-libperfmgr/aidl/SupportManager.cpp
--- a/power-libperfmgr/aidl/SupportManager.cpp
+++ b/power-libperfmgr/aidl/SupportManager.cpp
@@ -174,10 +174,6 @@ bool SupportManager::modeSupported(Mode type) {
         return false;
     }
     bool supported = HintManager::GetInstance()->IsHintSupported(toString(type));
-    // LOW_POWER handled insides PowerHAL specifically
-    if (type == Mode::LOW_POWER) {
-        return true;
-    }
     if (!supported && HintManager::GetInstance()->IsAdpfProfileSupported(toString(type))) {
         return true;
     }
